From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: div652 <div652@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:48:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(subagent): a settlement watcher failure no longer ends
 the process

Host teardown can dispose a child's session projections before the continuation
registry closes its Activation. The watcher's next settlement read of the child's
Inbox then throws ('cannot read inbox state: its projection registration is not
active'); the watcher ran as an unawaited async IIFE, so the rejection was
unhandled and the CLI exited with a fatal load failure. Catch it and log a warning:
the watcher has nothing left to settle.

Seen on Harvey FK-250 with Sol high and subagents on (tasks 136 and 152): the root
agent ran out of 429 retries and its teardown crashed instead of exiting cleanly.
---
 .../subagent/subagent/src/continuation-activation.ts     | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/subagent/subagent/src/continuation-activation.ts b/packages/subagent/subagent/src/continuation-activation.ts
index 782332b..b0d5ecb 100644
--- a/packages/subagent/subagent/src/continuation-activation.ts
+++ b/packages/subagent/subagent/src/continuation-activation.ts
@@ -728,7 +728,14 @@ export class ContinuableActivationRegistry {
         }
         return
       }
-    })()
+    })().catch((error: unknown) => {
+      // Host teardown can dispose the child's session projections before this registry closes the
+      // Activation; the settlement read of its Inbox then throws. The watcher has nothing left to
+      // settle, and an unhandled rejection here would end the whole process as a fatal load failure.
+      this.ctx.logger.warn(
+        `subagent "${activation.childId}" settlement watcher stopped: ${errorChain(error)}`,
+      )
+    })
   }
 
   /** Classify one Inbox and owned-child observation without reading Agent execution state. */
